summary:
  A track from My Music, an episode or an alarm leaves the last audition
  standing, so the next bare Play brings back a search result nobody was
  listening to any more.

history:
  The audition outranks lastPlay in the bare Play's decision, because a row
  deletion resets lastPlay to 0 behind the listener's back. That precedence
  is only right while the memory means "an audition was the last thing
  heard"; startWithFade is where every other kind of start forgets it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          if (root._previewUrl === "") root._lastAudition = null;

replace:
          if (false) root._lastAudition = null;

expect:
  Killed by test_invariants::test_only_an_audition_is_remembered_and_every_other_start_forgets_it.
  Line-neutral.
